#X text 240 83 generates a random value with a Gaussian distribution.
It has the shape of a bell curve and is characterized by two parameters
\, mu and sigma;
#X text 240 138 the center of the density function \, mu \, is the
mean of the random variable. The spread of the density function is
measured by a parameter called *standard deviation* or sigma. 68.26%
of all results fall within the interval of width ±SIGMA centered on
the mean: the random variable is unbounded both above and below the
mean;
#X text 240 239 99.74% of all results fall within ±3 SIGMA;
#X text 240 264 use the @seed property to get reproducible sequences.
If @seed is not set explicitly \, a generator initialized with the
current time is used;
#X text 240 319 the object can be used to add natural-looking random
variation \, for example to humanize timing and velocity or to simulate
measurement noise;
